Z||000004||falconhulk||08-21-2001||03:11 PM||||I used woodgrain contact paper on a project along time ago........just my opnion dosent look like it belongs.  When I did it it covered up original woodgrain insets.  To me this just looks out ofplace on the fiero inserts.  There is no molding lip to give it depth.  I really like the hood bird though....where did you get it?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gomez||08-21-2001||03:44 PM||||I think it looks pretty good. I may have to search thru the contact papers myself to see what I find.<P>Coarse gotta get the car on the road first.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bigpacupacu||08-21-2001||07:53 PM||||Thanks for the feedback. And yes I do think it looks pretty cool.<BR>I wish I could get better pics that aren't so fuzzy and grainy. The pics really do not do it any justice. I really wanted to find a cheaper way to get that"wood grain look". I went to Home Depot to find wood grain contact paper and saw a few different styles of wood. I then saw the black marble and white marble and said to myself "thats different". For $5.00 a roll of 15 feet of contact paper I figured "what the heck".If I dont like it ,I can just peel it off and try something else. I just stuck it on and cut around the holes and edges with a razor knife. It looks great to me! Maybe later I'll put a clear coat over it and make it a little more glossy.<P>Oh, FALCONHULK, its not a "hood bird", its the fiero pegasus logo. I got from FIEROGRAPHIX.COM. I think thats the right web site.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bigpacupacu||08-21-2001||07:54 PM||||Thanks for the feedback. And yes I do think it looks pretty cool.<BR>I wish I could get better pics that aren't so fuzzy and grainy. The pics really do not do it any justice. I really wanted to find a cheaper way to get that"wood grain look". I went to Home Depot to find wood grain contact paper and saw a few different styles of wood. I then saw the black marble and white marble and said to myself "thats different". For $5.00 a roll of 15 feet of contact paper I figured "what the heck".If I dont like it ,I can just peel it off and try something else. I just stuck it on and cut around the holes and edges with a razor knife. It looks great to me! Maybe later I'll put a clear coat over it and make it a little more glossy.<P>Oh, FALCONHULK, its not a "hood bird", its the fiero pegasus logo. I got from FIEROGRAPHIX.COM. I think thats the right web site.<P>------------------<BR>Steven Poole<BR>85GT 4sp||||reg||1
